posts.text:
🏠 Everyone talks about building more homes. Almost no one talks about whether federal mortgage policy is adding fuel to the fire.

If more government-backed financing creates more buyers while housing remains limited, what happens to prices?

@allenmendenhall is a Research Fellow in Economic Policy Studies and Senior Advisor for the Free Enterprise Initiative at The Heritage Foundation.

@votejohngibbs is the Director of Economic Policy Studies at the Heritage Foundation.

